            {
                "entry_id": "a73e3d47-f4e4-3c50-a746-2fffaa753005",
                "word": "Shanxi",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "16f4a480-9577-3fa1-8a09-3280779d6eb9",
                        "entry_id": "a73e3d47-f4e4-3c50-a746-2fffaa753005",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Province du nord-est de la Chine, dont le chef-lieu est Taiyuan."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ff62396-2f9f-4a4b-978f-89f932e884da",
                                "sense_id": "16f4a480-9577-3fa1-8a09-3280779d6eb9",
                                "text": "Le changement de couleur spectaculaire qui s’est produit sur le lac salé de Yuncheng, dans la province chinoise du Shanxi (ouest du pays), est un phénomène naturel …."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b3e1b611-c7d4-4146-8954-20375ffa0236",
                        "source_entry_id": "a73e3d47-f4e4-3c50-a746-2fffaa753005",
                        "source_sense_id": "16f4a480-9577-3fa1-8a09-3280779d6eb9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Shanxi",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shanxi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                        "entry_id": "92e5589f-6435-3dac-85ad-2031565a9534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A province in the northern part of China. Capital: Taiyuan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8f93f13-78a8-4adb-9721-513dff871115",
                                                "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                                "text": "Shi-whang-ti having obſerv’d in viſiting his Empire that the Northern Provinces, eſpecially Pe-che-li, Shan-ſi, and Shen-ſi, were much expoſed to the ſudden Incurſions of the Tartars ; he fent a formidable Army, which having driven them back a great way beyond the Frontiers of the Empire, he immediately put in Execution the Scheme he had form'd to ſecure his Country againſt ſuch dangerous Neighbours, by building a Wall from the Sea to the Extremities of the Province of Shen-ſi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34534737-3be9-46e8-87c9-e69d1c505f60",
                                                "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                                "text": "The Tachai Production Brigade is part of the Tachai Commune in Xiyang County, Shanxi Province, in Northern China. It’s tucked away in the Taihang Mountains, a bit over two hundred miles southwest of Peking, in an area with poor soil, serious erosion, and rock-strewn, mountainous terrain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec765988-d30a-4b7f-b76f-0bed1cd76389",
                                                "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                                "text": "First-phase liquefaction and storage facilities are in Qinshui county, Shanxi province while the second phase is in nearby Yangcheng county. Shanxi is the nation's largest coal-producing region accounting for about 25 per cent of the nation's output."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e427f81-d5d2-4d9b-a7d1-c50d52be93f1",
                                                "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                                "text": "Mr. Xi began proclaiming his dream since taking power five years ago, though he focused much of his early efforts on battling corruption. In Shanxi, the province that includes Datong, investigators have arrested so many corrupt cadres that the national government has declared the region to be in a state of “implosive corruption.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0d08f5b-921a-402e-aa1d-8ffb466bb0ec",
                                                "sense_id": "bca4d76f-bb19-343a-8736-232dc25ea3e2",
                                                "text": "A fire at a coal company's office in China's northern Shanxi province on Thursday killed at least 25 people and injured dozens more, according to Chinese state media.\nShanxi is a major coal-producing hub in China."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shanxi",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                        "entry_id": "387312c4-0901-3ba4-8dd4-c8c67d174805",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Shaanxi, a province in northwestern China. Capital: Xi'an."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "proscribed"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ca52ee1-264f-4cd5-9389-cdbda40f018b",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "The \"Yenan Period,\" 1935-1947, was the decisive decade of the Chinese Revolution.*[…]\nLiu Bao-zhei had helped create the Yenan spirit; he had joined the Eighth Route Army in 1937, leaving his home in Henan Province to fight the Japanese in the North. We met Liu on a state farm nestled in the Nanniwan Valley, near Yenan. His face, rough and creased, reflected many years of labor in the harsh climate of northern Shanxi Province. Liu wore a towel tied about his head in the traditional peasant fashion of the area."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6c51d0f-0e02-4d66-b093-311c5bcaa512",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "My survey deals with the ancient silk road between the former Changan, now Xian in Shanxi (Shanhsi) Province, proceeds to the Gansu Province and finally to the Uighur Autonomous Region of Xinjiang. It is primarily the Northern route which led through the land of the Mongols, Tibetans and Uighurs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "739aabae-f6d7-4912-86c6-e9c2f0feaeb5",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "After the Red Army sets up headquarters at Yanan in north Shanxi province, he accepts a frontline post in repelling the Japanese invasion, and becomes commander of the New Fourth Army."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e50ecc91-0651-4f45-a5d2-4a0dd7f969a0",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "A fervent believer in an afterlife, Qin Shihuang ordered his tomb to be guarded by 8,000 terra-cotta statues. This grandiose resting place was accidentally disinterred in 1976 by farmers digging a well in the ancient capital, Xian, during a drought.\nDr. Huang broached the idea of a terra-cotta exhibit on a trip to Shanxi Province, where Xian is located, three years ago."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c286d93-f7b3-4d9d-a452-2c68b56fc046",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "Owing to soil erosion, some farmland has become totally barren. In Chenjiagedu Village, Fugu county, Shanxi Province, since all farmland was lost, the local people were obliged to travel several kilometers for fertile soil.",
                                                "translation": "Lü you ying yu jiao cheng",
                                                "english": "Lü you ying yu jiao cheng"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "39433134-565f-4bfe-bbf6-b2a2197b4112",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "634 ·The Palace of Great Clarity, an imperial resort including residential and official buildings, is constructed northwest of Chang’an in Shanxi Province.\n636 ·The Zhaoling (Clarity Tomb) of Emperor Taizong is built in Liquan County, Shanxi Province. The tomb includes the well-known stone sculpture Six Horses of the Clarity Tomb."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3839eac-83bf-4582-aadc-3c77eed41264",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "In China, an outbreak of endemic human selenosis was reported in Enshi District, Hubei Province, and in Ziyang County, Shanxi Province, during the 1960s."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64e9839d-27c8-4ff1-a66d-f6ba202ece03",
                                                "sense_id": "21aa6548-396b-3fc3-9cd3-20a82500d48d",
                                                "text": "Production around the town of Ankang, a hundred miles south of Xian in Shanxi province, dropped by 25 per cent."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
